<article class="env-lemma" id="0AY5">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0AY5">Lemma <span data-tag="0AY5">31.13.10</span>.</a> Let $X$ be an integral locally Noetherian scheme. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a coherent $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module. The following are equivalent </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$\mathcal{F}$ is reflexive, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
for each $x \in X$ one of the following happens 
</p>
<ol>
  <li><p>
$\mathcal{F}_ x$ is a reflexive $\mathcal{O}_{X, x}$-module, or 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$\text{depth}(\mathcal{F}_ x) \geq 2$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
